From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <github@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] user_manager: give every Android app a webOS app

Android was one tile that opened a launcher. Upstream already does the hard
part - userUnlocked() enumerates packages through IPlatform.getAppsInfo(),
packageStateChanged() fires on install and removal, and icons are extracted
to ~/.local/share/waydroid/data/icons/<pkg>.png - it just emits .desktop
files, which webOS has no use for.

webOS finds applications by scanning the directories in sam-conf.json, each
holding an appinfo.json whose id is the directory name. So this writes one
such directory per launchable package, next to the .desktop file rather than
instead of it, so the same tree still works on a freedesktop host.

The ids matter beyond the launcher. hwcomposer sets the Wayland app_id of a
window to "Waydroid" for the full UI and "waydroid.<package>" for a per-app
window, and luna-surfacemanager carries that through to
WebOSSurfaceItem::appId; matching the webOS app ids to those is what lets the
card switcher show an app's own title and icon instead of an anonymous card,
and what lets SAM launch, track and close it.

SAM builds its application list once at startup and has no rescan -
com.palm.applicationManager/rescan belongs to the legacy manager and does not
reach it - so a set that has actually changed needs sam.service restarted.
That is why the emission tracks whether anything changed rather than
restarting on every unlock: at boot the directories are already on disk from
the previous session and nothing is restarted at all.

Kept to four functions so a rebase onto upstream only has to re-apply the
calls to them.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
